# ---- divergence D24: an earlier condition that fails only over the value over no rows ----

# The proof passes a condition that rejects nothing on its way to one that rejects the value over no rows, so the join
# back is INNER and antb1 never computes the earlier one for cities 4 to 6: it answers 1 2 3. DuckDB computes the
# conjuncts in the order written and fails. Over COUNT, over SUM under COALESCE, with a semi join between the two
# conditions, and an overflow. Written the other way round both engines answer (correlated_values.slt).
onlyif antb1
query I nosort
SELECT c.ct_id FROM cities c
WHERE CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city = c.ct_id) - 1 AS USMALLINT) >= 0
AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city = c.ct_id) > 0 ORDER BY 1
----
