statement error nope
SELECT c.ct_id, (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city < c.ct_id) AS n FROM cities c ORDER BY nope

# ---- select items under LIMIT (ADR 0041's SQ5b) ----

# Without ORDER BY the LIMIT keeps two rows, and both engines compute the items only for those (DuckDB at one thread,
# as the runner runs it), so the casts that would fail for later cities are never computed. Which rows a LIMIT without
# ORDER BY keeps depends on the plan (the outer side's order through a LEFT join back, which keeps it; an INNER one
# built on its left does not), hence rowsort. With ORDER BY every row's item is computed, and both engines fail.
query II rowsort
SELECT c.ct_id, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city = c.ct_id) - 1 AS USMALLINT) FROM cities c LIMIT 2
----
SMALLINT	USMALLINT
1	76
2	76

query II rowsort
SELECT c.ct_id, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city = c.ct_id) - 1 AS USMALLINT) FROM cities c
WHERE c.ct_id <= 3 OR c.ct_id = 6 LIMIT 2
----
SMALLINT	USMALLINT
1	76
2	76

# The item reads WHERE's value, whose INNER join back is built on its left, so the LIMIT may keep other cities than
# DuckDB's: every city WHERE keeps casts, and every projected row is alike, so the answer is the same either way.
query II rowsort
SELECT c.ct_id * 0 AS z, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city = c.ct_id) - 77 AS USMALLINT) * 0 AS v
FROM cities c WHERE (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM riders r WHERE r.rd_city = c.ct_id) > 0 LIMIT 2
----
SMALLINT	USMALLINT
0	0
0	0

statement error out of range for the destination type UINT16
