# Under an EXISTS the select list of a derived table or a CTE right under it is dropped, as DuckDB drops it, but a
# correlated value's join back stays in that block's slot, so its aggregate is computed: one that overflows fails antb1
# alone (DuckDB answers 1 to 6), as an uncorrelated value's does (select_values.slt). The subquery's own item above the
# join back is dropped unread, so an item that overflows fails neither engine.
onlyif antb1
statement error Overflow in addition of
SELECT c.ct_id FROM cities c WHERE EXISTS (SELECT * FROM (SELECT z.zn_id, (SELECT MAX(t.tr_rider + 9223372036854775807)
FROM trips t WHERE t.tr_pickup = z.zn_id) AS m FROM zones z) x) ORDER BY 1

